    <summaries>
      <summary>
        <versionCode>00</versionCode>
        <actionDate>2025-09-03</actionDate>
        <actionDesc>Introduced in House</actionDesc>
        <updateDate>2026-09-09T18:23:55Z</updateDate>
        <text><![CDATA[<p>This bill directs the Transportation Security Administration (TSA) to develop guidelines to improve access to a Transportation Worker Identification Credential (TWIC) for prisoners prior to their release.</p><p>Specifically,&nbsp;TSA must develop guidelines to assist individuals in federal, state, and local prisons in (1) pre-applying or preparing an application for&nbsp;a TWIC card; and (2) requesting an appeal or waiver of a preliminary determination of ineligibility for a TWIC card.</p><p>As background, a TWIC card is required by the Maritime Transportation Security Act for workers who need access to secure areas of U.S. maritime facilities and vessels. TSA conducts a background check to determine a person’s eligibility and issues the credential.</p>]]></text>
      </summary>
    </summaries>
